1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,526
Federal agents freed an outlaw to help

2
00:00:02,536 --> 00:00:03,425
them catch killers.

3
00:00:03,655 --> 00:00:05,188
Instead, he became one.

4
00:00:05,418 --> 00:00:07,933
Drumright, Oklahoma, 1924.

5
00:00:08,483 --> 00:00:11,171
In the 1920s, Osage people were being

6
00:00:11,181 --> 00:00:12,672
murdered for their oil wealth.

7
00:00:12,902 --> 00:00:14,730
It came to be called the Reign of Terror.

8
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:17,451
Agents let a bank robber named Blackie

9
00:00:17,461 --> 00:00:19,843
Thompson out, to work as their informant.

10
00:00:20,073 --> 00:00:21,635
He went back to robbing banks.

11
00:00:22,185 --> 00:00:26,202
On July 2, 1924, a bank in nearby Avery

12
00:00:26,212 --> 00:00:26,826
was robbed.

13
00:00:27,056 --> 00:00:29,100
Word came the robbers were headed toward

14
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:29,548
Drumright.

15
00:00:29,998 --> 00:00:32,425
Four officers went after them, all in one

16
00:00:32,435 --> 00:00:32,724
car.

17
00:00:32,954 --> 00:00:35,476
Near Drumright, the robbers opened fire on

18
00:00:35,486 --> 00:00:35,740
them.

19
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:37,834
The police chief was wounded.

20
00:00:38,064 --> 00:00:40,876
Officer Ulysses Lenox, 38, was killed.

21
00:00:41,826 --> 00:00:43,850
Blackie Thompson kept robbing banks.

22
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,976
In 1934, he broke out of death row in

23
00:00:46,986 --> 00:00:49,228
Texas, and was gunned down himself.

24
00:00:49,878 --> 00:00:51,921
Comment your town, and it could be next.

